      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "**Tokenizers**\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "They need to \"translate the text to numbers\". There are 3 types of tokenizers:  ![image.png](data:image/png;base64,)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Ikyr3HT-cE6f"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Word-based *tokenization*\n",
        "\n",
        "The idea is to split text by spaces or other rules like punctuation.\n",
        "Each word has a specific number or \"ID\", attributed to it.\n",
        "There are a lot of words in vocablurary and because of that to contain ids of all words will take up a lot of space. People decided to skip some inimportant word and mark them as unknown, also dont give another id to each form of word, because they have similar meaning.\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "Nhx5uDAfcmhw"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Character-based *tokenization*\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        " idea to split the text by the characters. every character has unique id. this way we can embede all words using few ids than in word-based tokenization!  But this type also have disadvabtages. we dont hold an information about whole word.  Also texts tokenized by character tokenization take out a lot of space.\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "DqbmI_vBedHP"
      }
    }
